{"qid":"Q184","names":["Republic of Belarus"],"title":"Republic of Belarus","endonym":{"native":"Беларусь","lang":"be"},"capsule":"The Republic of Belarus declared sovereignty in July 1990 and independence in August 1991 following the dissolution of the Soviet Union. Alyaksandr Lukashenka, elected president in 1994, consolidated authoritarian control through constitutional referenda in 1995 and 1996 that expanded presidential powers. Following a disputed presidential election in August 2020 that triggered massive protests and brutal suppression, the EU, United States, and other Western governments ceased to recognise Lukashenka as legitimate, while Belarus aligned itself more closely with Russia, which deployed troops from Belarus in its 2022 invasion of Ukraine.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Belarus's international borders are formally defined by Soviet-era administrative boundaries recognised at independence and are well documented, though the political situation since 2020 has affected international recognition without altering the physical territory.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Belarus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belarus"},{"label":"Wikipedia: 2020 Belarusian presidential election","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Belarusian_presidential_election"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Alexander Lukashenko","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Lukashenko"}],"britannica":"place/Belarus","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Belarus","rulers":[{"qid":"Q1361912","name":"Viačasław Kiebič","start":1991,"end":1994,"image":"Вячеслав Францевич Кебич.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.w